  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Which pair of numbers does not have a product equal to \\(36?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\{-4, -9\\}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\{-3, -12\\}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\left\\{\\dfrac12, -72\\right\\}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\{1, 36\\}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\left\\{\\dfrac32, 24\\right\\}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Two factors with opposite signs have a negative product. In choice C,\n\\[\\frac12\\cdot(-72)=-36,\\]\nwhich is not \\(36\\). Checking the other choices gives\n\\[(-4)(-9)=36,\\qquad(-3)(-12)=36,\\]\n\\[1\\cdot36=36,\\qquad\\frac32\\cdot24=36.\\]\nThus the required pair is \\(\\{\\frac12,-72\\}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm C\\).",
